1
00:24:24,579 --> 00:24:26,960
 Please take your seat and kindly silence your phones

2
00:24:26,960 --> 00:24:28,980
 and feel free to borrow insights outside

3
00:24:28,980 --> 00:24:30,819
 for simultaneous interpretation.

4
00:24:31,099 --> 00:24:31,819
 Thank you.

5
00:30:18,099 --> 00:30:28,960
 Welcome to day two of the review meeting of the ROC Taiwan's FIPS CEDAW report, and we're

6
00:30:29,960 --> 00:30:56,779
 And now to begin, over to the chair of the international review committee.

7
00:31:05,099 --> 00:31:11,380
 Thank you very much and good morning.

8
00:31:12,200 --> 00:31:18,759
 We express to you our appreciation for the cooperation of yesterday, for the hospitality,

9
00:31:19,599 --> 00:31:25,940
 and for the high level of engagement of government departments and also the civil society.

10
00:31:25,940 --> 00:31:31,680
 We thank you very much, honorable minister, for the courtesies that you've extended to us.

11
00:31:31,680 --> 00:31:32,579
 We are grateful.

12
00:31:33,339 --> 00:31:46,039
 And today we will proceed as scheduled on the agenda, reviewing articles 10 to 12.

13
00:31:46,039 --> 00:32:00,980
 And for that exercise, for that session, I'm going to be calling on colleagues who are leading on those articles to present questions,

14
00:32:01,539 --> 00:32:07,200
 and then we will open the floor for responses from government at this point.

15
00:32:07,200 --> 00:32:09,740
 So, Professor Niklas, you have the floor.

16
00:32:10,119 --> 00:32:10,200
 Thank you.

17
00:32:16,039 --> 00:32:20,720
 Thank you very much, Madam Chair.

18
00:32:21,339 --> 00:32:23,539
 Good morning, everyone.

19
00:32:23,539 --> 00:32:37,599
 It is a great honor to be back once again here in Taipei and with the task to review the implementation of the CEDAW Convention.

20
00:32:39,339 --> 00:32:48,140
 This time we are conducting the review in a changed global political environment.

21
00:32:48,140 --> 00:32:59,160
 We experience a new situation where big states and their leaders do not respect the international rule-based forms of cooperation,

22
00:32:59,519 --> 00:33:05,539
 but think that they freely can break the rules and conduct policies by force, threat,

23
00:33:05,880 --> 00:33:13,039
 and without respect for the rule and law and the international conventions on human rights.

24
00:33:14,519 --> 00:33:26,700
 Finland, my own country, and Taiwan both have the common feature that we have strong neighboring states

25
00:33:26,700 --> 00:33:32,619
 that are not so much concerned about human rights and the rule of law principles.

26
00:33:32,619 --> 00:33:46,619
 And I think that in such a situation it is extremely important for small democratic countries to maintain a strong commitment to human rights,

27
00:33:47,460 --> 00:33:58,440
 which help to create a resilient and inclusive society which can stand united in any crisis situation.

28
00:33:59,440 --> 00:34:15,119
 We have been asked by some NGOs what credibility the International Review Committee has and whether we have any kind of accountability

29
00:34:15,119 --> 00:34:22,119
 and that we should not make recommendations that go against the public opinion.

30
00:34:22,119 --> 00:34:33,119
 I therefore want to remind you all of the fact that universal human rights often may go against public opinion

31
00:34:33,659 --> 00:34:38,619
 and that they form basic consistent values.

32
00:34:39,980 --> 00:34:49,360
 The whole background for the UN human rights system is the experience of what can happen when the so-called public opinion

33
00:34:49,360 --> 00:34:58,940
 have been mobilized to aggression and hate towards different ethnic groups, other religions, nationalities,

34
00:34:59,840 --> 00:35:06,900
 especially the experience from the Second World War was behind this human rights system.

35
00:35:08,559 --> 00:35:13,619
 We in the Review Committee are independent experts on CEDAW.

36
00:35:13,619 --> 00:35:23,579
 Our task is to bring in the genuine and prevailing interpretation of the CEDAW Convention into this debate with the State Party.

37
00:35:24,179 --> 00:35:32,260
 This is also the base on which our work can be evaluated and for this we are accountable.

38
00:35:32,960 --> 00:35:41,579
 I now want to pose some questions on education where Taiwan has a quite robust system in place.

39
00:35:41,579 --> 00:35:50,599
 I only have three points to make about education, Article 10 in the CEDAW Convention.

40
00:35:52,159 --> 00:36:09,340
 First, we commend you for having followed the recommendation of the 2022 review by introducing since 2023 gender-related studies at three universities.

41
00:36:09,340 --> 00:36:22,599
 Our concern, however, is that the funding for these gender-related studies has been granted for three years.

42
00:36:23,380 --> 00:36:34,340
 Our concern is what will happen next and will there be continuation of such funding now when the three years are passing.

43
00:36:35,599 --> 00:36:52,400
 If the activities in these programs, if they have been successful, can you inform us about the situation with these university studies, what will happen next?

44
00:36:53,400 --> 00:37:06,239
 Second, we commend you for the encouraging of girls in the STEM areas of education with good results.

45
00:37:08,019 --> 00:37:15,360
 The technological challenges related to future university teaching are, however, big.

46
00:37:15,360 --> 00:37:29,900
 The technology makes the use of online teaching cheap and universities are pressed to include an increasing amount of online studies in the curriculum.

47
00:37:31,239 --> 00:37:44,039
 At the same time, AI is bringing and to some extent already has brought about huge changes in the use and creation of knowledge.

48
00:37:44,039 --> 00:37:51,619
 These changes are likely also to have gender implications.

49
00:37:53,000 --> 00:38:11,280
 Are you planning to study these implications in order to make sure that the new technology will not have negative consequences for equality in the educational system?

50
00:38:13,280 --> 00:38:26,019
 My third concern relates to the fact that we are still not convinced that the government is doing enough to facilitate the education of vulnerable groups.

51
00:38:27,500 --> 00:38:37,519
 We think about stateless children to migrant workers which are reported to only get elementary education until they get 15.

52
00:38:37,519 --> 00:38:46,539
 We think of teenage mothers leaving education and falling outside the educational system.

53
00:38:47,739 --> 00:39:03,559
 We think of girls and young women with disabilities still facing many problems and constraints, although there has been an increase in the funding for education for people with disabilities.

54
00:39:04,559 --> 00:39:14,139
 Can you tell us something of your plans to further enhance the education of these vulnerable groups of women and girls?

55
00:39:14,719 --> 00:39:16,320
 Thank you, Madam Chair.

56
00:39:20,480 --> 00:39:22,539
 Thank you very much, Nicholas.

57
00:39:22,539 --> 00:39:36,900
 I will now yield the floor to the head of the delegation to provide responses to the three core questions that were raised on Article 10.

58
00:39:37,079 --> 00:39:38,599
 Thank you. You have the floor.

59
00:39:44,500 --> 00:39:45,539
 Good morning, everyone.

60
00:39:47,519 --> 00:39:49,980
 I would like to thank the reviewers for the questions.

61
00:39:49,980 --> 00:39:59,980
 I think these three questions are focused on education, so I would first like to delegate to the Ministry of Education to answer comprehensively.

62
00:40:01,219 --> 00:40:15,039
 And because there are mentions of high-end research and gender, female-related, we're going to ask NSC to follow up.

63
00:40:15,039 --> 00:40:29,980
 And because AI was also mentioned about its gender implication, and we're going to ask Moda to take up this question later on.

64
00:40:31,219 --> 00:40:32,480
 Thank you.

65
00:40:37,260 --> 00:40:40,860
 This is the Ministry of Education.

66
00:40:40,860 --> 00:40:49,699
 We're going to ask the Tertiary Education and Departments.

67
00:40:51,400 --> 00:40:56,699
 Hello, this is the Ministry of Education on Higher Education Department.

68
00:40:58,440 --> 00:41:03,980
 We supported the three-year funding.

69
00:41:04,280 --> 00:41:05,920
 It's not just the three-year.

70
00:41:06,099 --> 00:41:07,519
 It's a continuous funding.

71
00:41:07,519 --> 00:41:11,519
 For these three universities, we would like to delegate some responsibilities.

72
00:41:12,219 --> 00:41:17,400
 For example, campus gender campaign.

73
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:24,719
 We asked one of the universities in Kaohsiung to take up the campaign work.

74
00:41:24,840 --> 00:41:30,199
 In addition to research, outreach is also a very important part of their work.

75
00:41:30,199 --> 00:41:40,059
 And we continue to provide them funding and resources to these institutes for these research and outreach work.

76
00:41:45,880 --> 00:41:53,420
 And for vulnerable children and vulnerable groups, including stateless child children.

77
00:42:00,880 --> 00:42:11,420
 Regarding vulnerable children and preschool children and for elementary and middle school,

78
00:42:12,239 --> 00:42:21,679
 basically stateless children are based on humanitarian considerations.

79
00:42:21,679 --> 00:42:30,500
 We provide them an affordable educator service and provide them schooling services.

80
00:42:31,260 --> 00:42:39,519
 These are provided by local governments, and that's for preschool and elementary school and middle school.

81
00:42:40,159 --> 00:42:46,380
 Okay, it's not about the elementary school and middle school, but after middle school,

82
00:42:47,739 --> 00:42:57,380
 after the K-12, vulnerable groups, stateless child or women with disabilities,

83
00:42:58,760 --> 00:43:04,300
 what are their educational resources or protections after K-12?

84
00:43:05,219 --> 00:43:10,380
 Any protections provided or any ways for them to overcome their disadvantages?

85
00:43:11,340 --> 00:43:13,179
 I don't think you answered this question.

86
00:43:18,619 --> 00:43:24,380
 We would like to further follow up with this question regarding vulnerable children.

87
00:43:26,099 --> 00:43:35,280
 For high schools, we don't have regulations for the protection of these rights.

88
00:43:35,679 --> 00:43:39,639
 We will go back and look into it.

89
00:43:42,579 --> 00:43:44,119
 Thank you very much.

90
00:43:44,119 --> 00:43:49,119
 Anything else you would like to follow up at the Ministry of Education?

91
00:43:50,599 --> 00:43:51,940
 What about STEM?

92
00:43:53,619 --> 00:43:55,480
 Do you have anything to follow up on STEM?

93
00:44:02,500 --> 00:44:10,619
 So this is the Ministry of Education additional information on STEM on university campuses.

94
00:44:10,619 --> 00:44:13,960
 Yes, we do have a pilot program for that promotion.

95
00:44:14,300 --> 00:44:21,239
 We provide subsidies to female STEM programs for talent cultivation.

96
00:44:21,719 --> 00:44:25,739
 In the past three years, we have subsidized many schools and many teams.

97
00:44:26,159 --> 00:44:30,940
 The funding comes from not only government, but also businesses,

98
00:44:31,940 --> 00:44:35,940
 and also the program requires collaboration with businesses,

99
00:44:37,000 --> 00:44:42,260
 and also supports female researchers and students to commit to the program

100
00:44:42,260 --> 00:44:48,800
 to deepen and upholster STEM's friendly environment and support environment.

101
00:44:49,260 --> 00:44:54,039
 And then if they do have a higher female percentage in the program,

102
00:44:54,079 --> 00:44:59,139
 we would also add additional subsidiary to $1 million.

103
00:44:59,139 --> 00:45:02,099
 We are promoting this program.

104
00:45:02,340 --> 00:45:07,400
 However, with one program, they cannot drive the entire campus to change their program,

105
00:45:07,440 --> 00:45:12,500
 so we hope the program can further expand its scope to the entire environment,

106
00:45:12,920 --> 00:45:14,559
 entire school organization.

107
00:45:15,039 --> 00:45:20,739
 And about National Science Council, can you proceed to provide additional information?

108
00:45:21,099 --> 00:45:28,480
 So this is National Science Council, and like the Ministry of Education just said about STEM,

109
00:45:29,480 --> 00:45:39,480
 on university and colleges, faculties and researchers' program proposals,

110
00:45:40,179 --> 00:45:47,699
 research program proposals for female professors or pregnant researchers,

111
00:45:48,280 --> 00:45:55,639
 we have relevant benefits, which means that there are some supporting programs

112
00:45:55,639 --> 00:46:01,880
 so that the female professors don't have to worry about their career development.

113
00:46:02,340 --> 00:46:10,260
 So that measures will be incorporated into our subsidiary programs,

114
00:46:10,599 --> 00:46:15,920
 and also we have an innovative service platform for entrepreneurs.

115
00:46:16,099 --> 00:46:17,340
 The name is TTA.

116
00:46:17,340 --> 00:46:28,340
 So for female entrepreneurs, we provide on this platform incentives to encourage innovations.

117
00:46:29,679 --> 00:46:31,719
 That's the additional information I have.

118
00:46:32,300 --> 00:46:33,460
 Thank you.

119
00:46:33,679 --> 00:46:39,440
 Moda, Ministry of Digital Affairs, can you talk about AI's impact on gender?

120
00:46:39,440 --> 00:46:48,300
 And this is Moda, and about AI's impact as emerging new technology

121
00:46:48,300 --> 00:46:52,699
 would further exacerbate gender bias and discrimination.

122
00:46:53,159 --> 00:46:57,760
 And then we established AI-EC, its actual evaluation center,

123
00:46:57,960 --> 00:47:06,539
 with the core task to evaluate AI products and systems, accuracy and precision and fairness,

124
00:47:06,539 --> 00:47:09,219
 and cybersecurity evaluation.

125
00:47:09,599 --> 00:47:16,539
 And about fairness, we include gender equality and equality for people with disabilities.

126
00:47:17,199 --> 00:47:20,579
 We want to ensure that AI, while they are providing services,

127
00:47:21,000 --> 00:47:28,000
 the answer and the results provided would also be compliant with gender equality values.

128
00:47:28,619 --> 00:47:29,219
 Thank you.

129
00:47:29,219 --> 00:47:39,920
 It is advised that maybe Ministry of Health and Welfare can also talk about children's daycare

130
00:47:39,920 --> 00:47:48,099
 and support for women, and then also additional subsidy and support programs for vulnerable students.

131
00:47:48,639 --> 00:47:53,619
 Ministry of Welfare and Health, can you provide further information on that?

132
00:47:58,440 --> 00:48:04,579
 Ministry of Health and Welfare, with regard to education,

133
00:48:05,219 --> 00:48:14,079
 we follow the rules of Ministry of Education as for benefits provided to vulnerable groups.

134
00:48:14,280 --> 00:48:20,539
 We do have programs that would support vulnerable teens and children.

135
00:48:21,219 --> 00:48:21,960
 Thank you.

136
00:48:21,960 --> 00:48:31,800
 Ministry of Education, I think you do have a program that subsidizes STEM female talents programs

137
00:48:31,800 --> 00:48:34,559
 for universities and colleges.

138
00:48:35,000 --> 00:48:41,460
 Can you further elaborate on this STEM program, if you do have additional information to offer?

139
00:48:43,519 --> 00:48:44,579
 Thank you.

140
00:48:46,519 --> 00:48:53,820
 About this, in 2025 we are already providing these programs,

141
00:48:53,920 --> 00:49:02,840
 so we have approved around 21 universities and 44 programs.

142
00:49:03,380 --> 00:49:12,059
 And then also we are going to build environment that is friendly to diverse, gender diversity.

143
00:49:12,059 --> 00:49:20,059
 And also schools need to take proactive role in supporting female researchers and faculty researchers.

144
00:49:20,579 --> 00:49:26,940
 So for the female researchers, if they have their program approved and subsidized by us,

145
00:49:27,300 --> 00:49:35,619
 and then should this researcher become pregnant, and then they can actually further delay and defer the program,

146
00:49:35,860 --> 00:49:38,559
 and then they can return to the workplace.

147
00:49:38,559 --> 00:49:47,739
 And then also we provide system design and resource allocation, and also campus culture enhancement.

148
00:49:48,300 --> 00:49:54,559
 We want to encourage women and build a system that can really support their career development.

149
00:49:55,559 --> 00:50:02,360
 And for the resource allocation, we would like to encourage female students to engage in project studies

150
00:50:02,360 --> 00:50:08,440
 and enterprise internship and international exchange programs, and about campus culture.

151
00:50:08,719 --> 00:50:14,980
 We also need to create and build a friendly and safe campus culture.

152
00:50:15,179 --> 00:50:18,340
 This is something we are working on. Thank you.

153
00:50:20,820 --> 00:50:25,159
 Do we have additional information our colleagues would like to offer?

154
00:50:26,019 --> 00:50:27,840
 This is Ministry of Education.

155
00:50:27,840 --> 00:50:35,099
 I would like to add, because you mentioned about the children of people with disabilities,

156
00:50:35,579 --> 00:50:41,840
 we also have these education fee deductions for people eligible, depending on household income,

157
00:50:42,639 --> 00:50:52,559
 and then also the severity of the disabilities, and then a different deduction of education fees would be offered,

158
00:50:52,820 --> 00:50:55,019
 depending on the level of the disabilities.

159
00:50:55,019 --> 00:50:57,900
 Is there anything else in the interest of time?

160
00:50:58,559 --> 00:51:03,019
 Now I'm going to give the time back to our review board. Thank you.

161
00:51:05,179 --> 00:51:09,019
 Thank you very much. The delegation, I would now...

162
00:51:09,880 --> 00:51:10,760
 No, you're okay.

163
00:51:12,679 --> 00:51:14,840
 Any other follow-up questions?

164
00:51:18,200 --> 00:51:20,000
 Okay. Thank you very much.

165
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:29,780
 We will now proceed to Article 11, and I will still yield the floor to Niklas Braun to take Article 11, please.

166
00:51:29,820 --> 00:51:30,239
 Thank you.

167
00:51:34,659 --> 00:51:37,320
 Thank you, Madam Chair.

168
00:51:37,940 --> 00:51:44,719
 We now turn to Article 11 that deals with employment.

169
00:51:45,720 --> 00:51:56,719
 The general impression of the implementation of Article 11 is that progress in Taiwan is slow,

170
00:51:57,260 --> 00:52:07,559
 although the achievements regarding sexual harassment in workplaces and sexual assault have to be recognized.

171
00:52:07,800 --> 00:52:11,340
 These are important achievements.

172
00:52:12,340 --> 00:52:19,699
 Regarding employment, I have four areas of concern which I want to address.

173
00:52:22,059 --> 00:52:32,739
 The first concern is the implementation of the principle of equal pay for work of equal value.

174
00:52:33,740 --> 00:52:43,800
 First, I note that we do not see that the CEDAW standard which requires equal pay to be paid

175
00:52:43,800 --> 00:52:55,059
 not only to equal or for the same work, but also for work of equal value has been implemented.

176
00:52:55,059 --> 00:53:04,360
 This means that according to the CEDAW standard, we must be able to compare also different jobs

177
00:53:04,360 --> 00:53:09,320
 and assess whether they are of equal value.

178
00:53:09,639 --> 00:53:14,860
 And if that is the case, there should also be equal pay.

179
00:53:16,860 --> 00:53:24,059
 Is, for instance, the work of a nurse of equal value with the work of a typical male job,

180
00:53:24,280 --> 00:53:27,340
 a policeman or a worker in the fire brigade?

181
00:53:27,519 --> 00:53:36,099
 These are questions that can be posed in the context of the CEDAW approach,

182
00:53:36,099 --> 00:53:47,699
 but with your wording in the legislation, it is questionable whether it applies in these cases.

183
00:53:49,059 --> 00:53:54,659
 We also note that the wage gap in Taiwan is very persistent.

184
00:53:55,340 --> 00:54:01,159
 The government seems to recognize that increased wage transparency

185
00:54:01,159 --> 00:54:07,460
 is one important tool in fighting the pay gap.

186
00:54:08,760 --> 00:54:20,599
 But the measures that restrict this transparency only to big listed companies

187
00:54:23,059 --> 00:54:36,780
 where the paid amount of capital is more than 10 billion NT dollars is really a very high threshold.

188
00:54:38,699 --> 00:54:44,639
 Have you, for instance, reflected on introducing a right for the applicant of a job

189
00:54:44,639 --> 00:54:50,500
 to get information about the wages of his or her predecessor?

190
00:54:51,420 --> 00:54:57,519
 There is a widespread understanding that some of the wage gap is due to the fact

191
00:54:57,519 --> 00:55:05,239
 that women have lower wage demands than men when they enter into a new job.

192
00:55:05,239 --> 00:55:14,400
 And a right to information about what wages the predecessor was paid could remedy this problem,

193
00:55:14,860 --> 00:55:20,599
 and this is a right which has been introduced in many countries.

194
00:55:22,360 --> 00:55:29,219
 The principle of equal pay should also be implemented on the whole labor market,

195
00:55:29,219 --> 00:55:38,619
 not only in some segment which seems to be the case in the measures that you have been taking.

196
00:55:39,719 --> 00:55:48,900
 My second concern relates to the issue of balancing family, childcare, and work.

197
00:55:48,900 --> 00:55:59,659
 Here the recognition that something has to be done seems to be well established and accepted,

198
00:56:00,739 --> 00:56:07,239
 and the concern about the low birth rate in Taiwan is common,

199
00:56:07,900 --> 00:56:16,219
 and since 2018 you have a plan to remedy this.

200
00:56:17,619 --> 00:56:29,639
 We note, however, that the list of measures reported in the answer to the list of issues,

201
00:56:30,659 --> 00:56:41,639
 we note that there is a long list of different fragmented measures, and this is, of course, understandable.

202
00:56:41,639 --> 00:56:49,760
 But we still lack a vision for how to really solve this problem.

203
00:56:50,500 --> 00:57:01,280
 Are you aiming for an affordable, high-quality, universal, and non-profit public childcare service system,

204
00:57:01,880 --> 00:57:07,900
 or what is the real model which you have in mind?

205
00:57:10,380 --> 00:57:20,920
 Also, are we aiming for a system where fathers are taking a substantial responsibility for parental leave

206
00:57:20,920 --> 00:57:28,019
 and is an integrated part of the system? The steps in this direction have been quite slow.

207
00:57:28,019 --> 00:57:39,800
 For an outside observer, it seems that the system needs some streamlining in order to avoid excessive fragmentation,

208
00:57:40,480 --> 00:57:45,820
 but this is, of course, the modest impression for an outsider observer.

209
00:57:45,940 --> 00:57:53,880
 It is very difficult to measure the different individual steps that have been taken.

210
00:57:53,880 --> 00:58:02,260
 But I would like to get your views on these more principal issues.

211
00:58:02,960 --> 00:58:12,260
 The third area of concern relates to the migrant domestic workers.

212
00:58:13,880 --> 00:58:20,880
 We see no progress in the situation of migrant female workers,

213
00:58:21,219 --> 00:58:34,019
 and since we know that there are almost 300,000 of those existing in Taiwan, this is not a minor problem.

214
00:58:35,860 --> 00:58:46,280
 The problems for these groups have been largely documented and they have been addressed last time,

215
00:58:46,280 --> 00:58:53,019
 I think, in the report of the ICCPR and the ICCR,

216
00:58:54,460 --> 00:59:02,599
 and with an increased number of second-generation, stateless children, the problems are just increasing.

217
00:59:03,440 --> 00:59:13,619
 We also know that the ILO Convention 109 on the situation of domestic workers

218
00:59:13,619 --> 00:59:21,119
 gives a good model for how these problems could be handled and solved.

219
00:59:21,659 --> 00:59:28,300
 I think that from the point of view of the ILO Convention, this is really a serious issue,

220
00:59:28,300 --> 00:59:34,780
 and I really urge the government to try to take action on this.

221
00:59:35,780 --> 00:59:38,780
 My fourth concern...

222
00:59:53,780 --> 01:00:00,300
 The situation of them still needs improvement in the report

223
01:00:00,300 --> 01:00:04,559
 or in the answers to our issues and questions.

224
01:00:06,019 --> 01:00:11,539
 The Ministry of Labour reports that they have promulgated the administrative guidance

225
01:00:11,539 --> 01:00:17,079
 on reasonable accommodation in the workplace for persons with disabilities,

226
01:00:17,320 --> 01:00:22,219
 and these have been effective from July 1st to 2025.

227
01:00:22,219 --> 01:00:31,099
 This is very welcome, and there is also further guidance on this issue.

228
01:00:31,559 --> 01:00:37,000
 But I remind you that these are recommendations for employers,

229
01:00:37,519 --> 01:00:47,619
 but actually, under UN standards, the lack of such accommodation would amount to discrimination.

230
01:00:47,619 --> 01:00:54,820
 In your system, it is just a recommendation to do this adjustment.

231
01:00:55,360 --> 01:01:05,500
 I understand that if employers don't apply them, there are no consequences.

232
01:01:06,500 --> 01:01:21,400
 We also note with interest the national action plan on business and human rights,

233
01:01:22,500 --> 01:01:26,139
 which you also present in your answer.

234
01:01:33,980 --> 01:01:42,460
 The Ministry of Labour here has proposed an action item on promoting the reference guidelines

235
01:01:42,460 --> 01:01:46,880
 for enterprises on the prevention of forced labour.

236
01:01:46,880 --> 01:01:57,199
 I think this is very important in a situation where new technology brings about new forms

237
01:01:57,199 --> 01:02:02,380
 of exploiting vulnerable groups in the working life.

238
01:02:02,920 --> 01:02:08,860
 We have platform work, different forms of digital work.

239
01:02:08,860 --> 01:02:19,159
 We have different forms of what in international vocabulary has been called modern slavery,

240
01:02:19,780 --> 01:02:24,260
 which is related to forced labour.

241
01:02:27,540 --> 01:02:38,320
 We think that this action plan is very important, and this should be taken forward,

242
01:02:38,320 --> 01:02:47,800
 and it is also related to the question of migrant domestic female workers,

243
01:02:48,539 --> 01:02:58,000
 which are in a situation which is quite equal to those who risk forced labour,

244
01:02:59,000 --> 01:03:03,559
 because these people can also be exploited on the private sector,

245
01:03:04,000 --> 01:03:06,940
 and this is what you are dealing with here.

246
01:03:06,940 --> 01:03:13,599
 So we urge you to go forward with these activities,

247
01:03:13,599 --> 01:03:20,280
 and I just want to hear how you are dealing further with these questions,

248
01:03:20,320 --> 01:03:29,820
 and how you are dealing with different vulnerable groups on the labour market.

249
01:03:30,000 --> 01:03:31,159
 Thank you very much.

250
01:03:33,859 --> 01:03:39,199
 Thank you very much for raising those intersecting concerns.

251
01:03:39,599 --> 01:03:42,940
 I'm sure the delegation would have responses,

252
01:03:43,340 --> 01:03:48,980
 and I will turn the floor over to you for your consideration and replies.

253
01:03:49,079 --> 01:03:50,480
 Thank you.

254
01:03:54,339 --> 01:03:57,039
 Thank you very much.

255
01:03:57,039 --> 01:04:03,500
 Regarding Article 11, the reviewer had four main concerns,

256
01:04:03,940 --> 01:04:06,920
 mostly concerning the Ministry of Labour,

257
01:04:07,000 --> 01:04:13,159
 so I would like to invite the Ministry of Labour to elaborate on this.

258
01:04:14,440 --> 01:04:18,619
 And regarding the first question about equal pay for equal work,

259
01:04:18,619 --> 01:04:25,800
 we are going to ask if the FCC can answer this question,

260
01:04:26,320 --> 01:04:30,400
 and the Department of Gender Equality will also follow up.

261
01:04:31,940 --> 01:04:37,500
 The second question is about family care, child care, and work balance.

262
01:04:38,639 --> 01:04:44,199
 In addition to Ministry of Labour, which has already touched on it,

263
01:04:44,199 --> 01:04:48,699
 maybe Ministry of Education and Minister of Health and Welfare

264
01:04:48,699 --> 01:04:53,559
 can also pick up on the question regarding child care.

265
01:04:54,179 --> 01:04:59,340
 And finally, regarding the digital forced labour issue,

266
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:04,219
 MODA can answer this question as well.

267
01:05:04,860 --> 01:05:12,139
 And also Ministry of Economic Affairs can take the first and fourth question

268
01:05:12,139 --> 01:05:13,500
 at the end.

269
01:05:15,739 --> 01:05:17,639
 This is the Ministry of Labour.

270
01:05:20,400 --> 01:05:22,960
 This is the first time we are talking.

271
01:05:23,280 --> 01:05:28,579
 We are at the Department on Employment Equality.

272
01:05:29,099 --> 01:05:35,940
 I would like to thank the reviewers for providing us with these comments and questions.

273
01:05:35,960 --> 01:05:39,340
 First of all, about narrowing the wage gap.

274
01:05:39,340 --> 01:05:45,380
 We agree equal pay for equal work is about the equal value.

275
01:05:45,820 --> 01:05:50,420
 And when we talk about equal work and equal pay,

276
01:05:50,800 --> 01:05:57,219
 in order for different enterprises to understand what equal pay for equal work means,

277
01:05:57,639 --> 01:06:04,940
 in 2023 we came up with a checklist for our competent authorities

278
01:06:04,940 --> 01:06:13,639
 to see if the equal pay for equal work is in line with the definition internationally.

279
01:06:14,320 --> 01:06:21,179
 And for all the HR departments to understand the concept of equal pay for equal work,

280
01:06:21,460 --> 01:06:27,639
 and we will continue to reinforce this concept with the enterprises in Taiwan.

281
01:06:28,300 --> 01:06:32,880
 And further, regarding the transparency of wages,

282
01:06:32,880 --> 01:06:36,099
 in addition to it being reflected in our checklist,

283
01:06:36,460 --> 01:06:40,760
 we also asked for voluntary disclosement from the enterprises.

284
01:06:41,320 --> 01:06:44,739
 Currently, large companies that are listed,

285
01:06:45,639 --> 01:06:53,139
 companies that have a volume of net worth over 10 billion new Taiwanese dollars,

286
01:06:53,320 --> 01:07:01,320
 they must disclose their gender information and their pay information versus their gender.

287
01:07:01,320 --> 01:07:09,340
 And in addition to this self-checklist for equal pay for equal work for business entities,

288
01:07:09,739 --> 01:07:17,639
 we understand that it's not just for large corporates, but for smaller enterprises.

289
01:07:18,719 --> 01:07:24,260
 The central government is working with the local governments when we are doing our compliance visits.

290
01:07:24,260 --> 01:07:29,659
 We also send out this self-checklist for different companies

291
01:07:29,659 --> 01:07:36,039
 so that they all understand and have the concept of equal pay for equal work.

292
01:07:36,719 --> 01:07:46,380
 And as of June this year, we've issued over 36,000 checklists to these business entities,

293
01:07:46,380 --> 01:07:49,079
 so they understand this concept.

294
01:07:49,719 --> 01:07:56,980
 And reviewers also talked about family care and work balance, specifically the child care.

295
01:07:57,360 --> 01:08:07,659
 We really care about this in addition to reinforcing our measures for child care subsidies to the enterprises

296
01:08:08,660 --> 01:08:17,359
 to build child care facilities or building measures in addition to amending the acts.

297
01:08:17,800 --> 01:08:28,300
 We currently have a reward measure that is in the Legislative Yuan pending adoption and review.

298
01:08:30,180 --> 01:08:33,460
 And regarding the family and work balance,

299
01:08:33,460 --> 01:08:39,880
 we understand that the duty of care is not just on one single gender.

300
01:08:39,960 --> 01:08:50,800
 So this year we emphasize that dual gender participating in the family care is very important.

301
01:08:51,699 --> 01:09:02,300
 And we discussed with CSOs, and they've shared with us that when they are trying to balance family and work,

302
01:09:02,300 --> 01:09:09,380
 the care, time, and balance is issue.

303
01:09:09,420 --> 01:09:28,279
 So we are moving towards a more flexible value so that different genders can take parental leaves flexibly,

304
01:09:28,279 --> 01:09:33,279
 and they can care for family and work at the same time.

305
01:09:33,979 --> 01:09:41,079
 Starting from January 1st this year, we have a new parental care policy that is more flexible.

306
01:09:43,100 --> 01:09:53,180
 From January to June, we can see over 50% of male have applied for parental leave.

307
01:09:53,180 --> 01:10:01,659
 And in the past, men only accounted for one-third of the parental care,

308
01:10:02,039 --> 01:10:14,760
 but now we are amending the regulations so that we are formalizing the parental leave

309
01:10:14,760 --> 01:10:27,460
 so that we can reinforce the maternity checkup leave and parental leave can be reinforced for the male.

310
01:10:29,039 --> 01:10:39,479
 And from currently seven days to 14 days for these maternity checkup leaves,

311
01:10:39,479 --> 01:10:51,480
 and for parental leaves for both parents, it's six plus three months now for both parents.

312
01:10:52,319 --> 01:10:56,840
 And this is an amendment that's currently being reviewed at the Legislative Yuan.

313
01:10:57,180 --> 01:10:59,859
 That's for the family work balance.

314
01:11:00,319 --> 01:11:07,479
 And regarding the foreign domestic workers' rights in Taiwan,

315
01:11:07,479 --> 01:11:18,239
 after six sessions of listening from CSOs, employers, and families that hire domestic workers,

316
01:11:18,680 --> 01:11:29,480
 we have compiled six aspects of the rights and benefits that need to be protected for our foreign domestic workers.

317
01:11:29,979 --> 01:11:36,260
 And through our policies and administrative measures and tools,

318
01:11:36,659 --> 01:11:44,199
 we are going to put out comprehensive ways, which my colleague will follow up later.

319
01:11:44,520 --> 01:11:51,779
 We will spare no measures to protect the rights of foreign domestic workers.

320
01:11:51,779 --> 01:12:00,159
 And regarding workers with disabilities, right now we have administrative guidances,

321
01:12:00,699 --> 01:12:08,460
 but if the person with disabilities asks for adjustments and the employer says no,

322
01:12:08,779 --> 01:12:16,920
 in the past it has constituted discrimination, and according to our Employment Act, it's still a violation.

323
01:12:16,920 --> 01:12:28,720
 And we are now in the process of encouraging corporations to actively take measures to adopt,

324
01:12:29,359 --> 01:12:32,039
 and that's what we have done so far.

325
01:12:33,300 --> 01:12:40,000
 This is also from the Ministry of Labor, the Enterprise Development Office.

326
01:12:40,479 --> 01:12:46,560
 Regarding childcare in companies, in addition to public childcare,

327
01:12:46,560 --> 01:13:01,560
 we also encourage companies to provide childcare measures and facilities from 2002 to 2026.

328
01:13:01,560 --> 01:13:08,899
 On June 26, we have subsidized over 4,700 enterprises,

329
01:13:11,680 --> 01:13:19,920
 or 47 counts of business entities to provide childcare services and facilities.

330
01:13:21,199 --> 01:13:28,300
 And it's a figure up to 0.4 billion as of June this year.

331
01:13:29,300 --> 01:13:32,800
 I would also like to add, this is also from the Ministry of Labor,

332
01:13:33,340 --> 01:13:41,020
 we currently have 220,000 foreign domestic workers in Taiwan,

333
01:13:41,760 --> 01:13:52,079
 and we will further take inventory of the contracts that we have for them.

334
01:13:52,079 --> 01:14:02,079
 We asked CSOs to host seminars and workshops to discuss the implementations

335
01:14:02,699 --> 01:14:08,500
 and for the rights protections of the domestic workers.

336
01:14:09,039 --> 01:14:16,319
 We provide measures including, before they enter Taiwan, they must participate.

337
01:14:16,319 --> 01:14:25,119
 The employers must take part in a seminar before they bring in the foreign migrant worker,

338
01:14:26,300 --> 01:14:30,560
 and the migrant worker must also take part in the seminar.

339
01:14:30,880 --> 01:14:39,979
 Also at the service station, at the airport, we also have a consultation station.

340
01:14:40,359 --> 01:14:45,340
 And once they come into the country, we have a hotline, 1-995.

341
01:14:45,340 --> 01:14:55,199
 That's a 24-hour hotline providing bilingual consultation and complaint services.

342
01:14:55,619 --> 01:15:01,560
 We also have local government migrant worker consultation service centers

343
01:15:01,560 --> 01:15:06,779
 that conduct routine surveys, checkups for violations.

344
01:15:07,699 --> 01:15:14,539
 And if migrant workers, they are under labor and wage disputes and they need legal aid,

345
01:15:14,539 --> 01:15:22,699
 they can also access this support and service from these local centers,

346
01:15:22,819 --> 01:15:27,880
 and they may have maladaptions in terms of languages and communications.

347
01:15:27,920 --> 01:15:33,680
 So we also have digital learning trainings to provide the Mandarin training courses.

348
01:15:34,119 --> 01:15:40,779
 If they are seriously injured and require assistance,

349
01:15:40,779 --> 01:15:44,039
 we have settlement and assistance provided.

350
01:15:44,039 --> 01:15:48,819
 And in terms of social resources, we also subsidize local governments

351
01:15:48,819 --> 01:15:58,279
 to produce cultural programs that will help them adapt to life in Taiwan

352
01:15:58,279 --> 01:16:03,239
 to protect their life pre and post entering Taiwan.

353
01:16:03,659 --> 01:16:08,720
 And in terms of forced labor, as our viewer mentioned earlier, Ron,

354
01:16:08,720 --> 01:16:13,619
 we have our own guideline for forced labor,

355
01:16:14,460 --> 01:16:21,800
 and this was enacted in February this year,

356
01:16:22,060 --> 01:16:26,859
 and it's currently launched in various local governments.

357
01:16:27,260 --> 01:16:32,000
 And we work with the Ministry of Economic Affairs and a fishery agency

358
01:16:32,000 --> 01:16:37,720
 to conduct campaigns, hearings, and we conduct,

359
01:16:39,239 --> 01:16:46,859
 we made tools based on ILO 11 indicators regarding forced labor.

360
01:16:48,000 --> 01:16:53,500
 And also in terms where it implicates our criminal code and human trafficking law

361
01:16:53,500 --> 01:16:59,420
 and Basic Labor Act, we will continue to promote all of this.

362
01:16:59,420 --> 01:17:06,220
 The core indicator about forced labor is the detaining of their documents,

363
01:17:06,399 --> 01:17:12,220
 and in April this year we have amended our laws, our Employment Act,

364
01:17:13,000 --> 01:17:21,100
 which forbids the brokers or employers or anyone from detaining the documents

365
01:17:21,100 --> 01:17:25,239
 of these migrant workers under any reason.

366
01:17:25,239 --> 01:17:28,380
 And if they violate, there will be penalties.

367
01:17:28,939 --> 01:17:34,420
 That's our current amendments and measures right now,

368
01:17:34,420 --> 01:17:42,600
 and we will continue to follow up based on the spirit of the conventions.

369
01:17:43,619 --> 01:17:46,279
 Any additional information from the Ministry of Labor?

370
01:17:47,279 --> 01:17:53,619
 If not, we would like to ask the Financial Advisory Council

371
01:17:53,619 --> 01:17:57,239
 to provide additional information.

372
01:17:57,600 --> 01:17:59,260
 FSC, please.

373
01:18:02,560 --> 01:18:08,100
 FSC, would you like to take the first question?

374
01:18:08,600 --> 01:18:09,239
 Equal pay?

375
01:18:11,640 --> 01:18:15,380
 Do we have FSC representative here?

376
01:18:18,640 --> 01:18:26,619
 So the wage disclosure, FSC, listed companies, disclosure of pay,

377
01:18:26,699 --> 01:18:30,800
 do we have FSC representative?

378
01:18:32,000 --> 01:18:35,659
 I think I can step in to provide additional numbers.

379
01:18:35,659 --> 01:18:36,960
 This is the Ministry of Labor.

380
01:18:37,539 --> 01:18:44,460
 So in 2025, according to the results of the evaluation of business governance,

381
01:18:45,079 --> 01:18:51,859
 and then the indicator is 4.2 that whether the company has a policy in place

382
01:18:51,859 --> 01:18:56,859
 to promote diversified workplace and gender equality policies.

383
01:18:56,859 --> 01:19:04,520
 So in 2024, we incorporated company governance disclosure guideline.

384
01:19:06,239 --> 01:19:07,960
 So gender equality is factor in.

385
01:19:08,159 --> 01:19:12,260
 And then in 2025, the average score of the business,

386
01:19:12,779 --> 01:19:17,119
 that average score is 89.78 percent.

387
01:19:17,380 --> 01:19:22,600
 So most of the listed companies have already disclosed their workplace

388
01:19:22,600 --> 01:19:26,979
 diversified policies and gender equality policies.

389
01:19:27,760 --> 01:19:29,619
 So it seems FSC is not here.

390
01:19:29,659 --> 01:19:33,619
 So we would like to ask the Department of Gender Equality

391
01:19:33,619 --> 01:19:40,319
 to provide additional information on the first question and the second question.

392
01:19:40,819 --> 01:19:44,199
 In the Ministry of Education, in the Ministry of Welfare and Health,

393
01:19:44,659 --> 01:19:49,939
 please provide your answer to daycare, work and life balance, career balance.

394
01:19:50,880 --> 01:19:54,859
 So with regard to workplace gender pay gap,

395
01:19:56,380 --> 01:19:59,940
 so Executive Yuan, we did observe a very big challenge.

396
01:20:00,800 --> 01:20:02,779
 That is our gender pay gap.

397
01:20:03,140 --> 01:20:07,079
 We cannot really gradually, steadily narrow that gap.

398
01:20:07,859 --> 01:20:12,340
 Department of Gender Equality conducted analysis,

399
01:20:12,500 --> 01:20:15,279
 and also we refer international frameworks.

400
01:20:15,279 --> 01:20:20,159
 So that gender pay gap do come with a lot of structural factors.

401
01:20:20,439 --> 01:20:24,199
 And then the result is that inequality of gender pay.

402
01:20:24,939 --> 01:20:28,520
 We don't have awareness of gender equality in workplace.

403
01:20:28,760 --> 01:20:32,539
 And then also the workplace is not friendly enough to women.

404
01:20:32,800 --> 01:20:40,180
 And also there are these like promotion ceilings vertically and horizontally.

405
01:20:40,260 --> 01:20:44,119
 And also there are different barriers between different industries.

406
01:20:44,119 --> 01:20:51,800
 And then that comes with a very big gender pay gap variance between different industries.

407
01:20:51,840 --> 01:20:58,840
 So we actually saw the gender pay gap inequality is the result of many folds of factors.

408
01:20:58,899 --> 01:21:05,260
 So we need to take a comprehensive and inter-administrative collaboration.

409
01:21:05,760 --> 01:21:10,199
 Therefore, we need to establish a gender-friendly workplace

410
01:21:10,199 --> 01:21:15,239
 and also empowering women's economic capability.

411
01:21:15,600 --> 01:21:19,439
 That is an issue for many ministries.

412
01:21:19,699 --> 01:21:27,539
 So we have strategies, for example, to narrow the horizontal and also the vertical gender segregation.

413
01:21:27,880 --> 01:21:32,500
 So we have programs to cultivate STEM female talents.

414
01:21:32,500 --> 01:21:41,100
 And then also National Science Council, Ministry of Education, and MODA would provide empower programs.

415
01:21:41,199 --> 01:21:45,300
 And also there are gender equality awareness workshops.

416
01:21:46,439 --> 01:21:54,380
 And then also we coach our listed companies to follow GRI to disclose their gender equality information.

417
01:21:54,380 --> 01:22:07,840
 And also we ask them to also cultivate prospects and potential female talents.

418
01:22:07,979 --> 01:22:11,579
 And also we want to cultivate a friendly workplace.

419
01:22:12,039 --> 01:22:16,439
 And then also vertically for the women, they would not hit a promotion ceiling.

420
01:22:16,439 --> 01:22:27,119
 And when it comes to gender pay gap in industries, we actually see there is a big gender pay gap when we compare different industries.

421
01:22:27,319 --> 01:22:36,039
 Therefore, we ask competent authorities to identify, for example, the manufacturing industry for electronic appliances.

422
01:22:36,640 --> 01:22:45,140
 These industries, they need, the competent authority of these industries need to provide measures to address this issue

423
01:22:45,140 --> 01:22:50,359
 and also provide further protection, advancement of women's workplace rights.

424
01:22:50,560 --> 01:22:54,920
 And also they need by stage aspects to disclose that information.

425
01:22:55,359 --> 01:23:05,039
 And then the pay gap data collection allows us to monitor the pay gap development over the years

426
01:23:05,039 --> 01:23:10,319
 as a basis for us to look into the issue so we can narrow the pay gap.

427
01:23:10,319 --> 01:23:17,699
 And also that data collection can help us to develop policy for equal pay promotion.

428
01:23:18,079 --> 01:23:20,279
 That is the work we have been doing here.

429
01:23:21,800 --> 01:23:25,939
 And Department of Gender Equality, have you covered all the grounds you want to cover?

430
01:23:26,500 --> 01:23:36,319
 Yes. Ministry of Welfare and Health and on daycare, maybe Ministry of Education can also provide further information on that.

431
01:23:37,440 --> 01:23:42,039
 MOEA, can you also chip in?

432
01:23:42,239 --> 01:23:51,979
 And MODA, you can also provide the digital forced labor issue as a Ministry of Health and Welfare.

433
01:23:52,739 --> 01:24:01,220
 Before I talk about daycare, so I would like to thank all the members of IRC for staying,

434
01:24:01,220 --> 01:24:05,659
 paying close attention to the low birth rate issue here in Taiwan.

435
01:24:06,399 --> 01:24:13,460
 In 2018, Executive Yuan has asked all ministries to pull resources together to address the issue.

436
01:24:14,159 --> 01:24:24,199
 So a daycare service is a critical element in that to help families strike a balance in parental obligations and job career balance.

437
01:24:24,199 --> 01:24:31,060
 So our goal is to establish public daycare services.

438
01:24:32,180 --> 01:24:42,420
 From 2021 to 2024, that public daycare services has grown by 53 percent.

439
01:24:42,720 --> 01:24:52,199
 And then also the daycare of children under two, that percentage has reached 56 percent.

440
01:24:52,600 --> 01:24:55,739
 And then also we want to publicize daycare services.

441
01:24:55,819 --> 01:24:59,060
 It takes time. We cannot do that overnight.

442
01:24:59,439 --> 01:25:12,819
 Therefore, at the same time, we utilize the quality private daycare centers and also at home daycare personnel to establish on par public daycare services.

443
01:25:13,000 --> 01:25:19,640
 As long as they are compliant with government standards, they can sign contracts with the government.

444
01:25:19,640 --> 01:25:32,579
 So the government can also leverage private resources to allow parents to enjoy these affordable daycare services with all these measures in place.

445
01:25:33,100 --> 01:25:43,739
 And then these child care daycare adoption rate for under two years old children has already grown to 56 percent.

446
01:25:43,739 --> 01:25:54,439
 And then when governments trying to advance this balance between parental obligation and job and work,

447
01:25:55,560 --> 01:26:02,640
 we also need to have supportive measures that drive for a friendly workplace.

448
01:26:02,640 --> 01:26:14,899
 And then from 2018 to 2025, and then we have already increased our budget to 120 billion.

449
01:26:15,739 --> 01:26:20,420
 And the Ministry of Education here at the Ministry of Education.

450
01:26:21,279 --> 01:26:26,899
 So additional information for preschool education and then like the Ministry of Education,

451
01:26:26,899 --> 01:26:32,979
 as our Ministry of Health and Welfare, we actually pull resources together across 12 ministries.

452
01:26:33,100 --> 01:26:39,939
 And then for these preschooler daycare that for year age two to five preschoolers,

