01:42:18,939 --> 01:42:25,500
 Regarding the question proposed, as we explained earlier on,

581
01:42:26,020 --> 01:42:34,859
 for business entities when they are promoting the right concept of equal work for equal pay,

582
01:42:34,859 --> 01:42:42,659
 we have a self-checklist and we have revised the checklist every year.

583
01:42:44,180 --> 01:42:50,800
 Two years before, we tell the business entities, you need to understand the job descriptions of each role,

584
01:42:51,279 --> 01:42:58,199
 not just looking at the same title, same job, and then you have the same pay.

585
01:42:58,800 --> 01:43:00,340
 It's not the same thing.

586
01:43:00,340 --> 01:43:08,420
 So we are taking steps to guide the business entities to understand, first of all,

587
01:43:08,819 --> 01:43:17,720
 understand their job descriptions, understand the values of these jobs, and to look at the standards of their pay.

588
01:43:18,140 --> 01:43:26,640
 And for all employees, when the employers are understanding the job description,

589
01:43:26,640 --> 01:43:33,140
 yes, we did not differentiate the paid and unpaid ratio.

590
01:43:34,439 --> 01:43:38,819
 But overall, after the first step, they understand the job descriptions,

591
01:43:38,960 --> 01:43:46,060
 then they can look at the pay that they provide for these jobs,

592
01:43:46,859 --> 01:43:52,640
 their differences in different gender or gender orientations.

593
01:43:53,359 --> 01:43:55,739
 That's the guidance right now.

594
01:43:55,739 --> 01:44:04,039
 And the next question, we also like to ask the Ministry of Labor to take about the penalty.

595
01:44:05,279 --> 01:44:11,079
 Basically, for the reasonable accommodation for disabled people, we do have a guideline.

596
01:44:11,319 --> 01:44:22,279
 In practice, I think our question in concern is actually the direct violation of Employment Service Act.

597
01:44:22,279 --> 01:44:27,279
 So we do have, in the past two years, actual cases in court that citation

598
01:44:27,819 --> 01:44:34,579
 because the employer refused to make reasonable accommodation for persons with disabilities.

599
01:44:34,739 --> 01:44:40,699
 In the ruling, the judge made it very clear it's a violation of the Fair Employment Act.

600
01:44:41,640 --> 01:44:47,640
 So the employee was employed, the contract was terminated.

601
01:44:47,640 --> 01:44:52,659
 So it was actually a lawsuit about employment.

602
01:44:53,340 --> 01:44:59,119
 So that termination of employment contracts is a violation against law.

603
01:44:59,819 --> 01:45:04,020
 Any additional information? If not, we're going to give the floor back to IRC.

604
01:45:04,279 --> 01:45:05,420
 Thank you.

