 But I guess it's voluntary, right?

2693
07:56:02,580 --> 07:56:08,299
 It's not mandatory after the couple goes through the mediation.

2694
07:56:08,819 --> 07:56:14,939
 If they feel they want to provide any feedback, they can.

2695
07:56:14,939 --> 07:56:21,099
 But you are not for sure collecting all the feedback

2696
07:56:21,099 --> 07:56:23,060
 or what is the system.

2697
07:56:25,060 --> 07:56:29,599
 After any mediation process,

2698
07:56:30,759 --> 07:56:34,400
 then you make sure that you collect feedback always,

2699
07:56:34,459 --> 07:56:35,540
 or is it voluntary.

2700
07:56:36,419 --> 07:56:43,940
 So if those women or men who went through the mediation process

2701
07:56:44,409 --> 07:56:49,250
 and then were fed up, really did not satisfy,

2702
07:56:49,669 --> 07:56:54,290
 but they might not give their feedback, which still happens.

2703
07:56:54,889 --> 07:56:59,229
 So I am asking whether it's mandatory requirement

2704
07:56:59,229 --> 07:57:02,490
 or is it voluntary to submit the feedback.

2705
07:57:02,689 --> 07:57:08,189
 I can understand that you are trying to collect the response afterwards.

2706
07:57:08,750 --> 07:57:10,930
 So that's one point.

2707
07:57:10,930 --> 07:57:21,889
 And then in case of before applying this protection order,

2708
07:57:22,369 --> 07:57:31,330
 I know that these days some men have a stalking habit,

2709
07:57:31,689 --> 07:57:38,409
 whether it's a divorced spouse or whether it's in a close relationship

2710
07:57:38,409 --> 07:57:42,569
 before marriage, stalking happens a lot.

2711
07:57:42,750 --> 07:57:48,369
 And then that might happen even between divorced couples.

2712
07:57:48,830 --> 07:57:59,389
 You divorce and then your former spouse is coming after you every day

2713
07:57:59,389 --> 07:58:03,869
 to your workplace, near your workplace, your new home, etc.,

2714
07:58:03,869 --> 07:58:06,770
 harassed by the telephone messages, etc.

2715
07:58:06,770 --> 07:58:17,569
 So there should be precautions after the couple went through the divorce,

2716
07:58:18,029 --> 07:58:20,250
 whether through litigation or mediation work.

2717
07:58:20,450 --> 07:58:24,650
 So we need all these precautionary measures.

2718
07:58:24,650 --> 07:58:37,650
 So in case the woman feels that she needs protection order before,

2719
07:58:38,689 --> 07:58:42,029
 after divorce, I think that should be given.

2720
07:58:42,430 --> 07:58:45,869
 So that would be my response for mediation,

2721
07:58:46,650 --> 07:58:48,630
 especially in case of domestic violence.

2722
07:58:49,409 --> 07:58:52,810
 And now this issue of alimony.

2723
07:58:52,810 --> 07:58:57,689
 I think Minister of Justice and Judicial Yuan,

2724
07:58:59,069 --> 07:59:06,650
 I think both agree that alimony should be canceled after remarriage of the spouse.

2725
07:59:07,270 --> 07:59:12,189
 And then you said that it applies both to men and women.

2726
07:59:12,409 --> 07:59:16,529
 Of course, the law should apply to both spouses.

2727
07:59:17,529 --> 07:59:24,369
 But I think it is disproportionately women who receive alimony,

2728
07:59:24,770 --> 07:59:30,130
 unless the woman is a rich millionaire.

2729
07:59:31,529 --> 07:59:38,450
 Usually it is women who are economically weaker and dependent upon the husband.

2730
07:59:38,990 --> 07:59:44,349
 So alimony applies the effect of cancellation of the alimony.

2731
07:59:44,349 --> 07:59:48,229
 Of course, it affects women disproportionately.

2732
07:59:49,689 --> 07:59:55,189
 So this cancellation of alimony, I don't know why you think it's complicated.

2733
07:59:56,450 --> 08:00:03,529
 And then what countries are you taking into account and studying the case?

2734
08:00:03,590 --> 08:00:10,189
 Because you said that you are also checking other countries' laws and systems.

2735
08:00:10,189 --> 08:00:17,349
 So may I ask which countries you are taking the example of

2736
08:00:17,349 --> 08:00:23,830
 in terms of cancellation of alimony upon remarriage after divorce?

2737
08:00:24,790 --> 08:00:30,250
 And then the first issue of division of residual marital property.

2738
08:00:30,610 --> 08:00:35,270
 I know that you are preparing and discussing with different ministries,

2739
08:00:35,270 --> 08:00:40,509
 different UNs, and then trying to come up with amendments so

2740
08:00:40,509 --> 08:00:46,049
 that the division of marital property applies to all occupations.

2741
08:00:46,450 --> 08:00:52,849
 So may I ask what kind of timeline do you have in mind?

2742
08:00:53,590 --> 08:00:56,209
 How long do you think the whole process would take?

2743
08:00:56,569 --> 08:01:01,270
 Because that might take ten years if there is no active

2744
08:01:02,990 --> 08:01:07,950
 measures taken or initiatives taken by the government.

2745
08:01:08,250 --> 08:01:10,750
 So that would be my response.

2746
08:01:10,849 --> 08:01:14,250
 And then I would wait for further replies.

2747
08:01:14,569 --> 08:01:15,849
 Thank you.

2748
08:01:21,090 --> 08:01:23,909
 So any responses from the delegation?

2749
08:01:24,650 --> 08:01:26,189
 Thank you.

2750
08:01:29,430 --> 08:01:30,790
 Thank you.

2751
08:01:31,169 --> 08:01:43,330
 Regarding these questions, the mediation, we would like to invite elaboration

2752
08:01:43,330 --> 08:01:50,709
 from the judicial union regarding the protection orders and mediation

2753
08:01:50,709 --> 08:01:54,790
 and if other ministries have things to elaborate.

2754
08:01:54,790 --> 08:01:59,490
 For example, stalking also has to do with the Ministry of Justice.

2755
08:02:03,169 --> 08:02:04,569
 This is about stalking.

2756
08:02:04,689 --> 08:02:09,369
 Maybe we can invite the Ministry of Justice to follow up.

2757
08:02:10,130 --> 08:02:13,130
 This is regarding mediation of divorce.

2758
08:02:14,529 --> 08:02:18,310
 And regarding the cancellation of alimony after remarriage,

2759
08:02:18,310 --> 08:02:26,369
 earlier on you mentioned that you were looking at other countries as well.

2760
08:02:28,890 --> 08:02:32,849
 And reviewers would like to know which countries are you looking at.

2761
08:02:34,090 --> 08:02:36,970
 Maybe the Ministry of Justice can elaborate on this as well.

2762
08:02:37,049 --> 08:02:43,770
 And finally, about the residual property division and alimony pension,

2763
08:02:43,770 --> 08:02:47,750
 this will be handled by the Department of Gender Equality.

2764
08:02:48,889 --> 08:02:51,950
 Thank you for your questions.

2765
08:02:53,110 --> 08:02:59,110
 This is from the Office of Tribunal and Family Affairs.

2766
08:02:59,669 --> 08:03:09,590
 Regarding the opinion and feedback from the plaintiff, is it mandatory?

2767
08:03:09,590 --> 08:03:20,369
 Usually these feedbacks or evaluation checklists would be provided to the

2768
08:03:20,369 --> 08:03:26,209
 plaintiff in the form of QR code, but in our family court affairs,

2769
08:03:27,810 --> 08:03:35,509
 the judge will do the final mediation and checking to sign the statement.

2770
08:03:35,509 --> 08:03:41,389
 So all of the family affairs mediation will be confirmed by the judge if in the process

2771
08:03:41,389 --> 08:03:59,389
 the plaintiff realizes that they are not, in fact, accepting of the requests made

2772
08:03:59,389 --> 08:04:02,069
 or the opinions made by the mediator.

2773
08:04:02,069 --> 08:04:08,069
 The plaintiff can respond to the judge at the end and the judge will personally

2774
08:04:08,830 --> 08:04:13,529
 chair the mediation to find the best way to mediate it.

2775
08:04:13,770 --> 08:04:16,490
 And secondly, when it involves the protection order,

2776
08:04:16,590 --> 08:04:24,509
 if it has to do with stalking and security, safety of the plaintiffs,

2777
08:04:24,849 --> 08:04:30,310
 in addition to provide, we will send a notification to the plaintiff

2778
08:04:30,310 --> 08:04:42,549
 so that they will know, they can notify the court that there are concerns of their security

2779
08:04:42,549 --> 08:04:53,049
 and the court can arrange for quarantine or separation so that there are no danger for them.

2780
08:04:53,049 --> 08:04:56,389
 And if danger happens within the courts,

2781
08:04:56,909 --> 08:05:02,349
 there are emergency bells installed in the mediation rooms.

2782
08:05:02,430 --> 08:05:06,549
 Once the marshals receive any notification,

2783
08:05:06,689 --> 08:05:10,229
 they will immediately provide assistance in the mediation room.

2784
08:05:10,770 --> 08:05:18,189
 And if they feel that they are concerned about their safety leaving the court,

2785
08:05:18,189 --> 08:05:21,669
 the local police can also assist.

2786
08:05:24,409 --> 08:05:28,509
 Would the judicial, the Ministry of Justice would like to elaborate,

2787
08:05:29,770 --> 08:05:36,189
 especially in terms of stalking or is it the responsibility of the Ministry of Interior?

2788
08:05:42,930 --> 08:05:47,709
 Okay, domestic violence falls under the jurisdiction of Ministry of Health and Welfare.

2789
08:05:47,709 --> 08:05:49,630
 Then we will invite the MOHW.

2790
08:05:50,090 --> 08:05:51,049
 Thank you very much.

2791
08:05:51,470 --> 08:05:55,909
 We would like to further elaborate that it was mentioned earlier, Ron,

2792
08:05:57,430 --> 08:06:05,509
 when the two parties are mediating or in the process of divorce

2793
08:06:05,509 --> 08:06:09,950
 and in addition to because of domestic violence,

2794
08:06:10,590 --> 08:06:13,770
 a protection order is filed, applied for,

2795
08:06:13,770 --> 08:06:19,110
 and if there are stalking issues, according to our Stalking and Harassment Prevention Act,

2796
08:06:19,529 --> 08:06:26,430
 we can ask police to file a written warning.

2797
08:06:26,610 --> 08:06:30,750
 And there are also safety plans that can be used.

2798
08:06:30,830 --> 08:06:36,290
 And there is also an app they can download that will help to locate them.

2799
08:06:36,389 --> 08:06:40,930
 And the police can know where they are to provide assistance in the case of emergencies.

2800
08:06:41,630 --> 08:06:42,689
 Thank you very much.

2801
08:06:42,689 --> 08:06:50,349
 Are there any other agencies who would like to elaborate on this domestic violence and stalking issue?

2802
08:06:50,630 --> 08:06:50,830
 No?

2803
08:06:51,049 --> 08:06:54,389
 Then we move on to the second question about alimony.

2804
08:06:54,930 --> 08:07:02,069
 And we would like to invite the Ministry of Justice to talk about the references they've been looking at.

2805
08:07:03,069 --> 08:07:06,849
 So we mainly looked at Germany and Switzerland.

2806
08:07:09,590 --> 08:07:19,950
 Their regulations say that if the other spouse remarries, the alimony will be canceled.

2807
08:07:20,270 --> 08:07:27,250
 But we must say that our draft is based on the court ruling right now.

2808
08:07:27,250 --> 08:07:35,130
 If the two parties they negotiate for,

2809
08:07:36,930 --> 08:07:41,970
 it depends on how the two parties negotiate on the alimony,

2810
08:07:42,409 --> 08:07:50,229
 or if it's just a one-off alimony payment, then it won't be limited to this.

2811
08:07:51,009 --> 08:07:52,849
 There will be no cancellation.

2812
08:07:52,849 --> 08:07:57,610
 And the cancellation is mainly about continuous or regular payments.

2813
08:07:59,049 --> 08:08:08,470
 Before the new marriage, they can receive the alimony.

2814
08:08:09,310 --> 08:08:13,610
 And whether or not this, because after remarriage,

2815
08:08:13,849 --> 08:08:21,590
 it's very difficult for the new spouse and the previous spouses to discuss the allocation of their child raising.

2816
08:08:21,590 --> 08:08:27,310
 And it's because there is a difficulty in this consideration,

2817
08:08:28,330 --> 08:08:37,549
 so we have included remarriage as one of the reasons for canceling regular alimony payment.

2818
08:08:38,810 --> 08:08:42,389
 Okay, are there any other explanations?

2819
08:08:42,889 --> 08:08:50,529
 If not, we go to the Department of Gender Equality for Residual Property Division.

2820
08:08:51,529 --> 08:08:59,790
 Now, when we talk about the timeline for the amendment in 2023,

2821
08:09:00,029 --> 08:09:02,330
 our cross-department consultation,

2822
08:09:04,049 --> 08:09:11,889
 it was decided that the Occupational Pension Act amendments

2823
08:09:11,889 --> 08:09:17,810
 will be amended individually by various competent authorities.

2824
08:09:17,810 --> 08:09:25,209
 And then we will amend them all together.

2825
08:09:26,270 --> 08:09:37,709
 And they will follow the Retirement Act for Public Servants and refer to the wordings.

2826
08:09:37,709 --> 08:09:50,169
 Now, this year, we further asked about the amendment for the Retirement Act for the Public Servants.

2827
08:09:50,490 --> 08:09:57,110
 And we learned that last year, Legislative Yuan passed a new amendment,

2828
08:09:57,509 --> 08:10:02,069
 which created impact to the pension system.

2829
08:10:03,069 --> 08:10:09,529
 And it caused some societal debates.

2830
08:10:09,869 --> 08:10:21,490
 Therefore, we're waiting for a further version to be provided to us

2831
08:10:21,490 --> 08:10:27,729
 to see by the Ministry of Personnel to see what the drafts are now.

2832
08:10:27,729 --> 08:10:34,889
 Are there any other agencies that would like to elaborate on the Division of Residual Property?

2833
08:10:35,290 --> 08:10:41,689
 If not, then we give the floor back to our reviewers. Thank you.

2834
08:10:45,229 --> 08:10:47,290
 Thank you very much, Honorable Minister.

2835
08:10:47,869 --> 08:10:50,209
 I just wanted a little clarification.

2836
08:10:51,209 --> 08:10:55,950
 You talked about remarrying and alimony,

2837
08:10:56,169 --> 08:11:00,369
 the conditionality is not being sustained because of remarriage.

2838
08:11:01,209 --> 08:11:03,029
 Rather than talking about remarriage,

2839
08:11:03,229 --> 08:11:07,049
 are there considerations within it about child care and child maintenance?

2840
08:11:07,409 --> 08:11:10,529
 Because often that's where the issue, the problem comes in,

2841
08:11:10,790 --> 08:11:16,849
 is that the burden of child care post-divorce is not well tidied up.

2842
08:11:16,849 --> 08:11:24,450
 And then remarrying then becomes a burden on usually the mother or one of the partners

2843
08:11:24,450 --> 08:11:30,029
 because this is not clearly stated in the alimony clauses or procedures.

2844
08:11:30,849 --> 08:11:32,430
 Is that clear in your own?

2845
08:11:33,029 --> 08:11:39,450
 Are there elements of child care that is clear in alimony and dissolution of marriage?

2846
08:11:39,770 --> 08:11:41,889
 Thank you.

2847
08:11:42,509 --> 08:11:43,130
 Professor Hisu?

2848
08:11:43,130 --> 08:11:50,130
 Actually, I was going to ask a similar question because you mentioned about child care included in the alimony.

2849
08:11:50,509 --> 08:11:52,889
 Alimony is different from child support.

2850
08:11:53,250 --> 08:12:00,630
 At the time of divorce, the court, if the divorce goes through the court legal procedure,

2851
08:12:01,110 --> 08:12:05,590
 then the court would say that the father, usually the father,

2852
08:12:06,029 --> 08:12:11,270
 will pay such and such amount monthly for the child support.

2853
08:12:11,270 --> 08:12:20,409
 And then some cases, the father doesn't care, even if he was ordered by the court,

2854
08:12:21,229 --> 08:12:27,250
 maybe a few months he will pay the child support, but afterwards he doesn't pay.

2855
08:12:28,090 --> 08:12:35,349
 So the former wife has a big problem in raising the child, which is completely different from alimony.

2856
08:12:36,350 --> 08:12:42,110
 Alimony is the compensation for the time lost by the wife

2857
08:12:42,110 --> 08:12:48,590
 because of her responsibility taking care of the house in terms of losing opportunity,

2858
08:12:49,110 --> 08:12:56,970
 all this losing capacity while the husband might, career-wise, continue to develop, etc.

2859
08:12:56,970 --> 08:13:09,009
 So I think the mixture within the concept of alimony, child care and child support, to me, it's not reasonable.

2860
08:13:10,150 --> 08:13:19,750
 And then as I talked privately with the bureau chief in the Department of Gender Equality in Korea,

2861
08:13:20,750 --> 08:13:27,169
 many fathers are just negligent of paying child care support.

2862
08:13:27,810 --> 08:13:34,549
 And then there is even a website created by men, by the way, saying bad fathers,

2863
08:13:34,810 --> 08:13:41,409
 and then they are chased and then their identification is exposed, and then out of shame,

2864
08:13:41,409 --> 08:13:46,689
 then the fathers started to repay the child support.

2865
08:13:48,009 --> 08:13:53,349
 It's bad fathers, of course, it's a private kind of social punishment.

2866
08:13:53,889 --> 08:14:04,529
 But anyway, that needs to be settled, whether the dissolution of marriage was settled between the spouses,

2867
08:14:04,529 --> 08:14:14,549
 okay, we divorce on our own, and then you will pay a certain amount monthly for the child or children that I am in charge of.

2868
08:14:14,810 --> 08:14:20,549
 Usually mother is given the child care responsibility after the divorce.

2869
08:14:20,669 --> 08:14:33,369
 That's the reality, which further obstructs her ability to seek employment and then to engage in other activities, etc.

2870
08:14:33,369 --> 08:14:43,549
 So that would be a question added by the chair's question regarding alimony and child support and remarriage.

2871
08:14:46,130 --> 08:14:47,569
 So back to you.

2872
08:14:48,369 --> 08:14:49,709
 Oh, thank you.

2873
08:14:52,389 --> 08:15:00,549
 Since we have time, I also want to ask something in relation to this alimony

2874
08:15:00,549 --> 08:15:06,669
 and the cancellation of the alimony in the situation of remarriage.

2875
08:15:07,130 --> 08:15:20,970
 I mean, if this kind of regulation will, of course, create a strong incentive not to formalize a relationship into marriage,

2876
08:15:20,970 --> 08:15:40,490
 or are you planning to have a regulation where you also can cancel the alimony in the situation where the lady has moved into a common household with a partner and have a relationship?

2877
08:15:40,490 --> 08:15:57,630
 So I mean, it is, in a sense, interesting to create mechanisms in the legislation where you, in a sense, put in obstacles for marriage

2878
08:15:57,630 --> 08:16:03,569
 because usually the society wants people to formalize the relationship.

2879
08:16:03,689 --> 08:16:09,330
 So I also think that this aspect has to be taken into account.

2880
08:16:09,330 --> 08:16:10,330
 Thank you.

2881
08:16:11,990 --> 08:16:13,650
 So back to you.

2882
08:16:13,650 --> 08:16:15,509
 Delegation, sir.

2883
08:16:19,270 --> 08:16:20,790
 Thank you.

2884
08:16:21,189 --> 08:16:33,049
 Obviously, upon remarriage, the issue do back further discussions, and when it comes to alimony, we also need to factor in the child support.

2885
08:16:33,150 --> 08:16:34,909
 These are two different things.

2886
08:16:34,909 --> 08:16:45,290
 However, it's possible that there is a need to continue to receive alimony or child support after remarriage,

2887
08:16:45,470 --> 08:16:54,169
 if that is obstructing them formalizing their relationship because they want to continue receiving the alimony or child support.

2888
08:16:54,250 --> 08:16:58,689
 Therefore, they would not consider formalizing their new relationship.

2889
08:16:58,689 --> 08:17:04,750
 So for the Ministry of Justice, would you like to further elaborate?

2890
08:17:07,830 --> 08:17:11,029
 So this is the Ministry of Justice.

2891
08:17:11,330 --> 08:17:13,430
 So we would like to further elaborate.

2892
08:17:13,430 --> 08:17:25,630
 When it comes to child support, like the review committee said, according to civil code that 21116.2,

2893
08:17:25,849 --> 08:17:35,590
 that the child support would not be canceled upon remarriage, and the elements constituting child support are different from alimony.

2894
08:17:36,229 --> 08:17:39,349
 Therefore, the remarriage would not cancel child support.

2895
08:17:40,350 --> 08:17:46,709
 So the former spouse would still need to continue to pay the child support.

2896
08:17:47,270 --> 08:17:56,909
 And then to answer the next part of the question, would that obstruct the formalization of a new relationship for one of the spouse?

2897
08:17:57,229 --> 08:18:06,209
 Again, I would like to emphasize, previously we talked about the claim to alimony would be terminated upon remarriage,

2898
08:18:06,209 --> 08:18:10,650
 but that is the regular alimony paid by installments.

2899
08:18:11,049 --> 08:18:13,150
 However, it's actually a lump sum payment.

2900
08:18:13,310 --> 08:18:16,889
 For example, according to the ruling, that would not be affected.

2901
08:18:19,150 --> 08:18:22,490
 Or they have a pre-negotiation on alimony payment.

2902
08:18:22,569 --> 08:18:23,669
 That would be not affected.

2903
08:18:23,770 --> 08:18:29,869
 Of course, one of the parties can evaluate, do they want to have the lump sum of the alimony?

2904
08:18:30,250 --> 08:18:35,830
 And if they are asking for the regular alimony payment, they need to consider the risks of the cancellation.

2905
08:18:35,830 --> 08:18:37,909
 Additional information.

2906
08:18:39,310 --> 08:18:55,090
 So I think we have a follow-up question from IRC about the systematic issue that obstructing formalization of marriage or just co-inhabitation.

2907
08:18:55,630 --> 08:19:02,830
 According to the draft we have for co-inhabitation, they are not formalizing a spousal relationship.

2908
08:19:03,319 --> 08:19:10,619
 Therefore, the alimony would not be canceled upon remarriage or entering into a co-habitation relationship.

2909
08:19:10,939 --> 08:19:14,319
 Thank you, Ministry of Justice, for the answer.

2910
08:19:14,560 --> 08:19:17,319
 Now we can give time back to the review committee.

2911
08:19:26,880 --> 08:19:30,740
 We had a very robust conversation.

2912
08:19:31,080 --> 08:19:32,220
 You still have a question?

2913
08:19:32,220 --> 08:19:33,299
 Yeah, you have the floor.

2914
08:19:33,500 --> 08:19:41,479
 Yeah, I asked which countries you took as an example, and you said that Germany and Switzerland.

2915
08:19:42,299 --> 08:19:52,220
 I think two countries are not universally applicable, so maybe you need to study more if you want to take into account the examples of other countries.

2916
08:19:52,500 --> 08:19:59,299
 And Germany and Switzerland, they all speak the German part.

2917
08:20:00,700 --> 08:20:02,979
 Northern Switzerland, they speak German.

2918
08:20:04,259 --> 08:20:07,639
 So similar social structures.

2919
